@startuml sequence_risk_assessment
title Figure 5a  Sequence Diagram — PLN-04 Assertion-level Risk Reasoning (P1)\n[Individual task · Member A]\nFrom the A1 node dispatch to the human decision at Gate_P1_step1: four-layer context assembly, LLM call,\nstructured output, four-level validation, StatePatch merge

skinparam defaultFontSize 20
skinparam legendFontSize 20
skinparam noteFontSize 18
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 560
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor White
  ParticipantBorderColor #444444
  ActorBackgroundColor White
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  ArrowColor #333333
  GroupBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  DividerBackgroundColor #E3EEFF
}

actor "RCA\n(human auditor)" as RCA
participant "A10 ConciergeAgent\n(separate StateGraph)" as A10
participant "A1 Orchestrator\n(StateGraph; StateQuery\n+ DecisionSubmit)" as A1
participant "A4 RiskAssessor\n(graph node)" as A4
participant "ProcedureLibrary" as PL
collections "Tier 2 Knowledge\n(standards fragments,\nclient profile)" as K
database "FinancialDataStore" as FDS
participant "LLMClient\n(LLMProviderAdapter)" as LLM
participant "JudgmentEngine\n(+ OutputValidator)" as JE
database "AuditTrail" as AT
database "AuditOutputStore" as AOS
database "CheckpointSaver" as CP

autonumber

== Node dispatch and procedure load ==

A1 -> A4 : run(state : EngagementState) : StatePatch
activate A4
note over A1, A4
  Agents never call each other (5.3). A1 hands over
  EngagementState; A4 returns a StatePatch. A1 itself
  never calls the LLM (4.1), and neither do A5 and A9.
end note

A4 -> A4 : selectProcedures(riskProfile) -> [PLN-04, ...]
note over A4, FDS
  This figure follows PLN-04 only. PLN-01, PLN-16, PLN-18 and
  the other P1 procedures of A4 take the same path; PLN-01
  supplies the proposed materiality shown at the gate below.
end note

A4 -> PL : load("PLN-04") : ProcedureTemplate
activate PL
PL --> A4 : engine = llm, autonomy_level = L2 (7.2)\nstandards = [ASA315 fragment (paragraph tbc, 4.3),\nASA240-P27]\ninputs, output_schema, context_budget\nprompt template
deactivate PL

== Baseline objectives — deterministic, no LLM ==

A4 -> FDS : query(trial balance)
activate FDS
FDS --> A4 : Row[]
deactivate FDS
A4 -> K : disclosure checklist (AASB 101 and\nstandard-specific disclosure items, 17.1)
K --> A4 : disclosure items

A4 -> A4 : baselineObjectives(trialBalance)\n-> AuditObjective[], origin = baseline
note over A4, LLM
  Rules enumerate material accounts x standard assertions plus
  disclosure items, so omission cannot occur by construction (P1).
  Revenue Occurrence and Cutoff carry fraudRelated = true and
  level = significant; these are preset and read-only for the
  LLM (ASA240-P27), which only rates and proposes additions.
end note

== Per-objective reasoning — one LLM call per procedure execution ==

loop for each AuditObjective (or batch of objectives)

  A4 -> K : fetch fragments in procedure.standards
  activate K
  K --> A4 : fragment text + fragment ids
  deactivate K

  A4 -> FDS : query(rows and columns from inputs)
  activate FDS
  FDS --> A4 : Row[]
  deactivate FDS

  A4 -> A4 : assemble prompt, four layers (8.5)
  note over A4, LLM
    1 System   role, output JSON schema, 8.3 constraints (fixed template)
    2 Standards  fragment text verbatim; pointers must cite fragment ids
    3 Task   prompt template + params + this objective and its RiskItem
    4 Data   rows and columns from inputs, prior_risk_register summary
    EngagementState itself never enters the prompt (8.5, 18.5).
  end note

  opt assembled size > context_budget
    A4 -> A4 : split into batches, one call each\nbatchNo into the trail, never truncate
  end

  A4 -> A4 : cacheKey = hash(engagement, procedure version,\ninput hash, evidence hash, prompt hash,\nmodel version)

  alt cache hit (3.4, 18.5)
    A4 -> AOS : read(cacheKey) : Judgment
    activate AOS
    AOS --> A4 : cached Judgment, LLM call skipped
    deactivate AOS
    A4 -> AT : log(cache hit, cacheKey)
  else cache miss
    A4 -> LLM : complete(prompt, outputSchema)
    activate LLM
    LLM --> A4 : rating, reasoning_chain,\nEvidencePointer[], c_llm,\nproposed added objectives
    deactivate LLM
    note over LLM, AOS
      API structured output enforces output_schema;
      temperature = 0 lowers variance, it is no guarantee.
    end note
    A4 -> AT : log(model version, full prompt,\ninput hash, params, tokens,\nlatency, batchNo)
  end

  loop until accepted, format retries at most 2
    A4 -> JE : validate(raw, output_schema)
    activate JE
    JE -> JE : validateSyntax -> validateStructure\n-> validateReferences -> validateSemantics
    alt syntax or structure invalid (8.6 levels 1-2)
      JE --> A4 : parse / schema error
      A4 -> LLM : complete(prompt + error, outputSchema)
      LLM --> A4 : corrected response, re-validated on the next pass
    else some pointers invalid (8.6 level 3)
      JE --> A4 : accepted; those steps marked unsupported and kept (8.3),\nevidence coverage reduced, the Judgment continues
    else no valid pointer, or semantic check fails (8.6 levels 3-4)
      JE --> A4 : accepted but flagged for a human (7.4 downgrade);\nnothing discarded, it still continues to buildJudgment
    else valid
      JE --> A4 : accepted
    end
    deactivate JE
  end
  break format retries exhausted
    A4 -> AT : log(validation exhausted)
    ref over A4, JE, AT
      Engine fallback: ProcedureRun failed, ReviewTask kind failed, no Judgment - Figure 5b
    end ref
  end
  note over A4, AT
    Scope: this break belongs to the per-objective loop, not to the
    validation loop above it. Only exhausted format retries end the
    execution here; the other three branches fall through to buildJudgment.
  end note

  A4 -> JE : buildJudgment(findings, PLN-04)
  activate JE
  JE -> JE : computeConfidence(judgment)
  note over JE, CP
    c_ev 0.3 and c_llm 0.2 apply. c_rule is hybrid-only and
    c_critic needs A7, which an L2 procedure does not use, so
    both weights fall to zero and the rest are renormalised (8.4).
    Confidence is never taken from the LLM on its own.
  end note
  JE -> AT : log(validation result, retry count)
  JE --> A4 : Judgment
  deactivate JE
  note over A4, AOS
    JudgmentEngine only builds the Judgment and returns it; it writes no
    business Store. A4 carries the Judgments in its StatePatch and A1
    writes them after mergePatch (18.5). The AuditTrail write stays immediate.
  end note

end

A4 -> A4 : rateRisks(objectives) : RiskItem[]\neach RiskItem.judgmentRef = {id, version};\nadded objectives get origin = llm_added

== Patch merge and checkpoint ==

A4 --> A1 : StatePatch { Judgments, audit_objectives, risk_register }
deactivate A4
note over A4, A1
  Nothing in the patch is in a business Store yet. The instance writes
  only the AuditTrail itself; every business result below is written by
  A1 once the patch has passed the four checks (18.4, 18.5).
end note

loop mergePatch, at most two attempts
  A1 -> A1 : four checks (18.3.1 authorisation, type,\nid uniqueness, foreign keys) (8.6)

  alt any check fails, first attempt
    A1 -> AT : log(merge rejected, failing check, patch discarded)
    A1 -> A4 : re-run once (new execution)
    A4 --> A1 : StatePatch (re-run)
  else all four pass
    A1 -> A1 : merge into EngagementState
    A1 -> AOS : write(Judgments, RiskItems, AuditObjectives)
    A1 -> CP : save(threadId, state)
    note over A1, CP
      Business Store first, checkpoint second (18.5). A checkpoint
      restores execution; it is not the audit trail behind M-07.
      The re-run that succeeds joins this same commit point.
    end note
  end
end

break both attempts failed
  A1 -> AT : log(merge rejected twice)
  ref over A1, A4, PL
    Execution marked failed, ReviewTask kind failed; the gate is not reached - Figure 5b
  end ref
end
note over A1, AT
  Scope: this break sits at the top level of the figure, outside the
  mergePatch loop. It ends the sequence - the gate below is never entered.
end note

== Gate_P1_step1 — PLN-01 / PLN-03, autonomy L1 ==

A1 -> A1 : interruptAt(Gate_P1_step1)\nmain graph suspended

activate A10

loop until an approve with a current targetVersion is written

  A10 -> A1 : queryState(engagementId, scope)
  A1 --> A10 : StateView: phase at Gate_P1_step1,\nproposed materiality, objective list,\nRiskItem levels, reasoning chains, confidence
  A10 -> RCA : notifies that the gate is reached (proactive, 5.5),\npresent(item) / explain(question)
  RCA -> A10 : confirms or edits each objective\nand RiskItem

  opt level changed, or revenue fraud presumption lowered
    A10 -> A10 : capture the reason verbatim; a lowered\npresumption also needs rebuttalReason
  end

  A10 -> A10 : collectDecision() -> build GateDecision\n(gate = PLN-01/03, targetId = risk_register vK,\ntargetVersion, decision, edits[], reason)
  note over RCA, A1
    A10 transcribes the structured fields; no LLM sits in the write
    path (18.5). One GateDecision per gate: targetId is the
    risk_register snapshot, per-item changes travel as edits[].
  end note

  A10 -> A1 : submit(GateDecision) : Result
  A1 -> A1 : check targetVersion and gate state

  alt targetVersion stale
    A1 --> A10 : re-present the current version,\nno new version created (18.5)
    A10 -> A10 : loop continues, the gate stays at Gate_P1_step1
  else d.decision = insufficient_info
    A1 -> A1 : gate stays open; the requested\nqueries or evidence are queued
    A1 --> A10 : re-present when the answers arrive
    A10 -> A10 : loop continues, the gate stays at Gate_P1_step1
  else d.decision = reject
    A1 -> A1 : append gate_decisions; edits[] become\nrework input, RiskItems keep their version
    A1 -> A4 : re-rate the edited items\n(Figure 3a: [d.reject] / applyEdits)
    ref over A1, A4 : per-objective reasoning above
    A1 -> A1 : loop continues, Gate_P1_step1 is presented again
  else d.decision = approve, version and gate state valid
    A1 -> A1 : append gate_decisions; apply edits[]:\nrevise(level, reason, user) on each edited\nRiskItem -> version + 1; write materiality,\nperformance_materiality, clearly_trivial
    A1 -> AT : log(human decision, dwell time)
    A1 -> CP : save; resume from interrupt
  end

end
deactivate A10
note over A10, A1
  Only the approve branch leaves this loop. Stale, insufficient_info and
  reject all re-present the current version at the same gate, so nothing
  below is reached without an approval bound to a current version (18.5).
end note

ref over A1, A4, PL
  Objective-level pack assembly, coverage gate, AuditPlan vN
  and the PLN-15 narrative, then Gate_P1_step2 — see Figure 4a
end ref

legend right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | Rectangle lifeline | Agent or support service (Figure 1b) |
  | Cylinder lifeline | Store or trail behind a contract interface |
  | Bar on a lifeline | The participant holds control |
  | alt / opt / loop | Branch, optional fragment, repetition |
  | break | Exit of the fragment it is drawn in, nothing below it runs |
  | ref | Detail shown in another figure |
  |= Invariant |= |
  | No agent-to-agent call | A1 passes EngagementState, A4 returns StatePatch (5.3) |
  | Human talks to A10 only | Reads via StateQuery, writes via DecisionSubmit (18.2) |
  | Business results are written by A1 after mergePatch | JudgmentEngine only builds them (18.4, 18.5) |
  | Only an approve leaves the gate | Stale, insufficient_info and reject re-present the current version (18.5) |
  | LLM at procedure granularity | One execution of one procedure is one call (8.5) |
  | Every call leaves a trail | Prompt, model version, hashes, tokens, validation (M-07) |
endlegend

@enduml
